{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/954803-medieval-setting-rules","id":954803,"title":"Medieval setting rules?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-20T21:26:51-07:00","id":954803,"title":"Medieval setting rules?","content":"I know that there are some rules for a medieval setting in Dark Eras, and in Mirrors, but I don't own those books. Can anyone give me the basics? I understand some of the skills are different, but does weapons like bows and crossbows negate your defense? How does plate armor work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T00:49:58-07:00","id":954877,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Medieval Rules</b><br /> <br /> You can find relevant playtest documents for the upcoming <i><b>Hurt Locker</b></i> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bH4XMrM7iovLQGBLJGVXHDTGXUrNc0JMy22wc-5MxZ8/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vnyL9EMa20a31vU48bvliUxsUxvphRaW8vg5K_xutrY/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. It been a while since this material was released and will likely have changed somewhat in the final version, but its a good place to get started for mechanics related to using archaic weapons and armor.<br /> <br /> The other main element of Era- Specific play is adjusting the Skill selection to fit the time period. For a Medieval game, I like the following substitutions <hr />From Mental skills, remove <i>Computers</i> and replace with one of the following as appropriate.<br /> <br /> <b>Enigmas: </b>Enigmas is the Skill for finding patterns in chaos. It is particularly useful for unravelling codes and cyphers, navigating complex systems \u2014 like arcane peerages or unwieldy bureaucracies \u2014 and cross-referencing large amounts of disparate information.<br /> <br /> <b>Travel:</b> Travel represents a character\u2019s knowledge of lands outside his own, from the trade routes it might take to get to the next country over to the sort of money they accept there or what the dominant religion is. Travel can be a vital skill in surviving abroad, particularly in the days before tourism guidebooks and chartered air travel. Note that this is a Mental Skill, not a Social Skill. Travel does not replace Persuasion, Socialize or Streetwise when actually dealing with foreigners, though a Travel roll may complement those rolls. This Skill is useful for both cultural and geographical knowledge. While Survival might be used to navigate short distances in the wilderness, Travel can be used to navigate longer distances via trade routes, astronomy or other measures.<br /> <br /> <b>Warfare: </b>This Skill represents a character\u2019s understanding, gained by education, experience or just innate sense, of large-scale tactical maneuvers. Warfare is useful when planning for a battle (to assign troops well, to read the lay of the land for potential advantages and trouble spots and to predict enemy movements) and when attempting to read the flow of events during open conflict. A character with a high rating in Warfare is unlikely to walk into a trap in battle, and is more likely to adopt the right response to a change in circumstances amidst the din and chaos of war.<br /> Warfare does not just represent the ability to gain objectives in war \u2014 it is the ability to gain those objectives while incurring a minimum of losses on one\u2019s side and inflicting a maximum of casualties on the enemy. Any good soldier can take an objective with overwhelming force. It takes a great one to achieve the same goal with an underpowered force and avoid losing any subordinates in the process. <hr />From Physical Skills, remove <i>Drive</i> and <i>Firearms</i>. Replace with the following.<br /> <br /> <b>Archery [Replaces Firearms]: </b>Archery allows your character to identify, maintain and operate most types of bows and crossbows. This Skill can represent formal military training or the familiarity born of experience in the field. Note that dots in Archery do not apply to manually fixing or building bows or fletching arrows, only to wielding them. Construction and repair are the province of the Crafts Skill.<br /> <br /> <b>Ride [Replaces Drive]:</b> The Ride Skill allows your character to control and guide a mount under dangerous or difficult conditions. Characters don\u2019t need this Skill simply to ride a horse, camel or other mount. Rather, this trait represents the training or experience necessary to maintain control at high speeds, to ride through dangerous environments without injuring the mount and to push the mount to the limits of its performance. Note that dots in Ride do not apply to training a mount, only to riding one. Taming and instruction of a mount are the province of the Animal Ken Skill.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 08-21-2016, 03:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T00:56:50-07:00","id":954878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/954803-medieval-setting-rules?p=954877#post954877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Re: Medieval Rules</b><br /> <br /> You can find relevant playtest documents for the upcoming <i><b>Hurt Locker</b></i> <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bH4XMrM7iovLQGBLJGVXHDTGXUrNc0JMy22wc-5MxZ8/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vnyL9EMa20a31vU48bvliUxsUxvphRaW8vg5K_xutrY/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. It been a while since this material was released and will likely have changed somewhat in the final version, but its a good place to get started for mechanics related to using archaic weapons and armor.<br /> <br /> The other main element of Era- Specific play is adjusting the Skill selection to fit the time period. For a Medieval game, I like the following substitutions <hr />From Mental skills, remove <i>Computers</i> and <i>Science</i>.<br /> Replace with the following.<br /> <br /> <b>Travel [Replaces Computers]:</b> Travel represents a character\u2019s knowledge of lands outside his own, from the trade routes it might take to get to the next country over to the sort of money they accept there or what the dominant religion is. Travel can be a vital skill in surviving abroad, particularly in the days before tourism guidebooks and chartered air travel. Note that this is a Mental Skill, not a Social Skill. Travel does not replace Persuasion, Socialize or Streetwise when actually dealing with foreigners, though a Travel roll may complement those rolls. This Skill is useful for both cultural and geographical knowledge. While Survival might be used to navigate short distances in the wilderness, Travel can be used to navigate longer distances via trade routes, astronomy or other measures.<br /> <br /> <b>Warfare [Replaces Science]: </b>This Skill represents a character\u2019s understanding, gained by education, experience or just innate sense, of large-scale tactical maneuvers. Warfare is useful when planning for a battle (to assign troops well, to read the lay of the land for potential advantages and trouble spots and to predict enemy movements) and when attempting to read the flow of events during open conflict. A character with a high rating in Warfare is unlikely to walk into a trap in battle, and is more likely to adopt the right response to a change in circumstances amidst the din and chaos of war.<br /> Warfare does not just represent the ability to gain objectives in war \u2014 it is the ability to gain those objectives while incurring a minimum of losses on one\u2019s side and inflicting a maximum of casualties on the enemy. Any good soldier can take an objective with overwhelming force. It takes a great one to achieve the same goal with an underpowered force and avoid losing any subordinates in the process. <hr />From Physical Skills, remove <i>Drive</i> and <i>Firearms</i>.<br /> Replace with the following.<br /> <br /> <b>Archery [Replaces Firearms]: </b>Archery allows your character to identify, maintain and operate most types of bows and crossbows. This Skill can represent formal military training or the familiarity born of experience in the field. Note that dots in Archery do not apply to manually fixing or building bows or fletching arrows, only to wielding them. Construction and repair are the province of the Crafts Skill.<br /> <br /> <b>Ride [Replaces Drive]:</b> The Ride Skill allows your character to control and guide a mount under dangerous or difficult conditions. Characters don\u2019t need this Skill simply to ride a horse, camel or other mount. Rather, this trait represents the training or experience necessary to maintain control at high speeds, to ride through dangerous environments without injuring the mount and to push the mount to the limits of its performance. Note that dots in Ride do not apply to training a mount, only to riding one. Taming and instruction of a mount are the province of the Animal Ken Skill.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank-you, you always have good information. <br /> Is their in depth rules for warfare? Does your defense apply to bows? I was considering using this for a song of ice and fire game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T01:09:31-07:00","id":954881,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Song of Ice and Fire</b><br /> <br /> Funny you should say that. I started putting together my own set of rules for doing a gritty fantasy SOIAF style game!<br /> <br /> The in-depth for Warfare is best detailed on pg.106 -107 of <i>Requiem for Rome</i>.<br /> <br /> Archery is treated the same as Firearms - targets do not use their Defense unless using an ability that dictates otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T08:32:12-07:00","id":954961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/954803-medieval-setting-rules?p=954881#post954881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Re: Song of Ice and Fire</b><br /> <br /> Funny you should say that. I started putting together my own set of rules for doing a gritty fantasy SOIAF style game!<br /> <br /> The in-depth for Warfare is best detailed on pg.106 -107 of <i>Requiem for Rome</i>.<br /> <br /> Archery is treated the same as Firearms - targets do not use their Defense unless using an ability that dictates otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not applying defense doesn't sound right. I bow were as effective as guns no one would have bothered with swords, axes, and plate armor. Where is your asoiaf stuff?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T09:46:17-07:00","id":954990,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Bowmanship</b><br /> <br /> In many respects, the force and penetration delivered by an arrow is superior to that of a bullet. And the velocity of atypical arrow means that evading an on-target arrow is very unlikely.<br /> One of the (many) reasons firearms usurped archery in warfare was less about overall effectiveness and move about efficiency. Riflemen were easier to train than Bowmen.<br /> <br /> So I generally agree with the system logic that a arrow has enough force and velocity to negate the advantage of training and reaction represented by Defense.<br /> However, Archery rules have been a point of contention for years. If allowing Defense against Archery has a better feel at your table, then go for it.<br /> <br /> <b>Re: SOIAF rules</b><br /> <br /> At this point, they are mostly brainstormed notes and ideas in a file folder, mostly to pin down the edges of the rules I want to use.I have even done a few write ups for dragons, direwolves and a couple of the characters. I haven't dug into the deep work of trying to convert Westeros to the CofD system. My current idea is to mostly run it as a mortals game, with merits for some of the more supernatural elements. I am somewhat undecided on whether to represent House affilitation with the Status Merit, or like Mystery Cult Initiation, which gives Merits and bonuses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T09:49:50-07:00","id":954993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/954803-medieval-setting-rules?p=954961#post954961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not applying defense doesn't sound right. I bow were as effective as guns no one would have bothered with swords, axes, and plate armor. Where is your asoiaf stuff?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a difference between not applying defence, and bows being as effective as guns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T09:56:48-07:00","id":955000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/954803-medieval-setting-rules?p=954990#post954990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Re: Bowmanship</b><br /> <br /> In many respects, the force and penetration delivered by an arrow is superior to that of a bullet. And the velocity of atypical arrow means that evading an on-target arrow is very unlikely.<br /> One of the (many) reasons firearms usurped archery in warfare was less about overall effectiveness and move about efficiency. Riflemen were easier to train than Bowmen.<br /> <br /> So I generally agree with the system logic that a arrow has enough force and velocity to negate the advantage of training and reaction represented by Defense.<br /> However, Archery rules have been a point of contention for years. If allowing Defense against Archery has a better feel at your table, then go for it.<br /> <br /> <b>Re: SOIAF rules</b><br /> <br /> At this point, they are mostly brainstormed notes and ideas in a file folder, mostly to pin down the edges of the rules I want to use.I have even done a few write ups for dragons, direwolves and a couple of the characters. I haven't dug into the deep work of trying to convert Westeros to the CofD system. My current idea is to mostly run it as a mortals game, with merits for some of the more supernatural elements. I am somewhat undecided on whether to represent House affilitation with the Status Merit, or like Mystery Cult Initiation, which gives Merits and bonuses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mystery cult seems more interesting, but a lot more work. It might work well as for example, the Lanister family has in common a high presence, and resources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T10:24:43-07:00","id":955012,"title":"","content":"Why not steal Dynasty Membership from Requiem and apply it to Houses instead of Clans?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T11:03:10-07:00","id":955024,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Dynasty Membership</b><br /> <br /> This is a good option, but may need to tweak the merit. Otherwise one dot gets a squire a +5 bonus for name dropping &quot;Tywin Lannister&quot;.<br /> <br /> One of the things I am considering is a framework that works just as well for Great Houses, Lesser Houses, and other organizations like the Night's Watch or the Order of Maesters","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T11:28:21-07:00","id":955035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/954803-medieval-setting-rules?p=955012#post955012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not steal Dynasty Membership from Requiem and apply it to Houses instead of Clans?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that from the core VtR book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T11:30:05-07:00","id":955036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/954803-medieval-setting-rules?p=955024#post955024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Re: Dynasty Membership</b><br /> <br /> This is a good option, but may need to tweak the merit. Otherwise one dot gets a squire a +5 bonus for name dropping &quot;Tywin Lannister&quot;.<br /> <br /> One of the things I am considering is a framework that works just as well for Great Houses, Lesser Houses, and other organizations like the Night's Watch or the Order of Maesters</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair I wouldn't take anyone lightly who works for Tywin \ud83d\ude09","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","user":"K9ine","date":". 08-21-2016, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T11:33:39-07:00","id":955044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/954803-medieval-setting-rules?p=955035#post955035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is that from the core VtR book?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I guess it would be a better model for the direct family members rather than extended house members.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T12:41:17-07:00","id":955096,"title":"","content":"try this one<br /> <br /> This is my first pass at an Affiliation Merit, modeled after the Mystery Cult Initiation Merit. Unlike Status (which represents overall authority and influence) this merits represents loyalty and dedication to the House or Organization. A minor sworn sword could have little status, but be fanatically dedicated, while a clever manipulator could have great influence but little loyalty. <br /> <br /> <b>Affiliation</b><br /> \u25cf \u2013 Associated; A Skill Specialty or one-dot Merit, pertaining to the lessons taught to initiates.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf \u2013 Loyal; A one-dot Merit.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf \u2013 Dedicated; A Skill dot, or a two-dot Merit<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf \u2013 Scion; A three-dot Merit<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf \u2013 Exemplar; A three-dot Merit, or a major advantage not reflected in game traits.<br /> <hr /><br /> <i>Example - </i><br /> <br /> <b>Affiliation \u2013 House Lannister</b><br /> \u25cf \u2013 Associated; The Lannister\u2019s reputation for chilling, brutal reprisals has rubbed off on you. You gain an Intimidate specialty in Revenge.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf \u2013 Loyal; You have benefited from the almost legendary wealth of House Lannister. You gain a dot in the Resources Merit.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf \u2013 Dedicated; Those affiliated with House Lannister are remarkably stubborn and willful. You gain the Iron Will Merit.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf \u2013 Scion; Lannister\u2019s gather power and influence almost instinctively. You may spend three dots between Contacts, Allies, Resources, or Retainers<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf \u2013 Exemplar; Your influence allows you to marshal the strength of House Lannister. Once per chapter, you may make a demand of any character with fewer dots of Status (House Lannister) than you. They gain the Tasked Condition. If they fulfill the demand, gain a Beat. The task must be something that would take at least a full day\u2019s work, or put the recipient in danger.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T14:52:55-07:00","id":955907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/954803-medieval-setting-rules?p=954961#post954961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not applying defense doesn't sound right. I bow were as effective as guns no one would have bothered with swords, axes, and plate armor. Where is your asoiaf stuff?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Defense and Armor are two different things. You still get Armor reduction but you can't dodge or deflect the incoming arrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T16:43:25-07:00","id":957266,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><i>Praise Sithrak for those houserules.</i></span></b></span></u></span><br /> <br /> On a less death, destruction and eternal fire and suffering note, I used nwod 1e+GM update for a dark low fantasy game (low as in &quot;people say once dwarf people lived here, these are their abandoned homes&quot; and &quot;these molten walls suffered the anger of the last dragon centuries ago&quot; kind of low) with lots of intrigue, actually not that unlike song of fire and ice, and the system works pretty good for that.<br /> <br /> I presented it to a group of players that while mature and used to different kinds of roleplaying experiences were used to fantasy games being about combat, and so the system helped a lot to drive home it was an intrigue game that just happened to be set on a fantasy setting. I also used Honor-based morality substitute (perceived honor, no less). As I said, worked wonders.<br /> <br /> Oh, and I also used the no defense rule for all projectile weapons because I really like how the Witcher Game of Imagination rpg does combat, and it uses something similar to that (he's got a bow aimed at you? surrender!). Also they had read the Archer's Tale books so I had to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11854-dibastet","name":"DiBastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T17:21:16-07:00","id":957279,"title":"","content":"A Medieval chronicles of darkness game its really easy to do.. fantasy settings like D&amp;D can be tricky, mostly because mages (The Mage game would feel out of place and the magic system would be too powerful i think).<br /> Would work pretty well with song of ice and fire and other low fantasy settings tough. borrow from Werewolf and make direwolves apply defense against ranged attacks. Maybe give some kind of vigor to giants to show how dangerous they are. Give dragons a good natural armor and make they ignore the bashing damage if they reduce the attack to 0.<br /> <br /> About houses, i would make a &quot;Noble&quot; merit (kind of similar to the Noble background from older games) one or two dots and you were one of those random lannisters that Robb Stark had in prison and five dots, well you could be Robb Stark himself depending of other merits, probably could be Rickon. the station that you are born is usually the most important thing on this kind of setting.<br /> <br /> The SOIAF rpg game is nice, especially because of the house mechanics. and they could be easily implemented or used in a SOIAF CofD game, i believe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12264-isengrim","name":"Isengrim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T21:59:34-07:00","id":957404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DiBastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/954803-medieval-setting-rules?p=957266#post957266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><i>Praise Sithrak for those houserules.</i></span></b></span></u></span><br /> <br /> On a less death, destruction and eternal fire and suffering note, I used nwod 1e+GM update for a dark low fantasy game (low as in &amp;quot;people say once dwarf people lived here, these are their abandoned homes&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;these molten walls suffered the anger of the last dragon centuries ago&amp;quot; kind of low) with lots of intrigue, actually not that unlike song of fire and ice, and the system works pretty good for that.<br /> <br /> I presented it to a group of players that while mature and used to different kinds of roleplaying experiences were used to fantasy games being about combat, and so the system helped a lot to drive home it was an intrigue game that just happened to be set on a fantasy setting. I also used Honor-based morality substitute (perceived honor, no less). As I said, worked wonders.<br /> <br /> Oh, and I also used the no defense rule for all projectile weapons because I really like how the Witcher Game of Imagination rpg does combat, and it uses something similar to that (he's got a bow aimed at you? surrender!). Also they had read the Archer's Tale books so I had to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like it works as well as I hoped. Thanks for sharing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T14:10:48-07:00","id":957835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/954803-medieval-setting-rules?p=955024#post955024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Re: Dynasty Membership</b><br /> <br /> This is a good option, but may need to tweak the merit. Otherwise one dot gets a squire a +5 bonus for name dropping &quot;Tywin Lannister&quot;.<br /> <br /> One of the things I am considering is a framework that works just as well for Great Houses, Lesser Houses, and other organizations like the Night's Watch or the Order of Maesters</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. What about Personal Status and House Status? Like, House Lannister has Status 5 (Westeros), while a mere Page or Squire might only have Status 1 (House Lannister). Among others of the same &quot;rank&quot;, the Lannister Page would be higher than, say, a Tarly.<br /> <br /> If more variation is desired, you could always have an Advanced tier to represent the true movers and shakers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-25-2016, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}